  "answer_text": "There are several entities associated with the name **\"Chase Capital Services\"** or similar names. Here is an overview of the most notable ones:\n\n---\n\n### 1. \ud83c\udfe6 JPMorgan Chase \u2013 Capital & Commercial Banking Services\nChase offers a broad range of financial services including credit cards, mortgages, commercial banking, auto loans, investing, and retirement planning.\n\nThrough its commercial banking arm, J.P. Morgan provides tailored credit, financing, treasury, and payment solutions for businesses of all sizes and commercial real estate, backed by the strength and stability of J.P. Morgan, with dedicated experts delivering industry-specific guidance and services.\n\nThey help clients achieve long-term strategic goals through financing, liquidity, payments, risk management, and investment banking solutions, including M&A, capital raising, and risk management for a broad range of corporations, institutions, and governments.\n\n---\n\n### 2. \ud83c\udfd8\ufe0f Chase Capital Holdings, LLC (Atlanta, GA)\nChase Capital Holdings, LLC is a trusted partner in the world of investment real estate financing, operating as a family-owned and operated boutique lending business based in Atlanta with 20+ years of expertise in the industry.\n\nTheir mission is to cater to the needs of experienced real estate investors throughout the Southeastern United States, offering quick and straightforward funding solutions for residential real estate investments.\n\n---\n\n### 3. \ud83c\udf31 Chase Capital (Canada)\nChase Capital is a private capital platform dedicated to investing in, advising, and helping unique businesses grow into dynamic platforms across Canada and other regions globally, bringing valuable capital and trusted industry expertise to acquisitions and partnerships with existing owners and operators.\n\nThey drive success in key growth sectors such as energy transition, waste & resource recovery infrastructure, and food & agricultural production, focusing on investments and partnerships in the energy sector to support sustainable and innovative projects.\n\nUnlike traditional private equity funds, they invest their own capital and collaborate with a network of experienced entrepreneurs and investors not bound by fixed exit timelines or rigid investment criteria, focusing on building long-term, sustainable value.\n\n---\n\n### 4. \ud83d\udcca Chase Capital Partners (Now Closed)\nThis firm's broad platform was positioned to deliver extensive product capabilities \u2014 including lending, treasury services, investment banking, and asset management \u2014 to meet clients' U.S. and international financial needs. However, Chase Capital Partners is permanently closed.\n\n---\n\nCould you clarify which **Chase Capital Services** you are referring to? For example:\n- Are you looking for **JPMorgan Chase** banking/capital services?\n- The **Atlanta-based real estate lending** firm?\n- The **Canadian private equity** platform?\n\nThis will help me give you more specific information!",
